condition_name: Lung Cancer
condition_slug: lung-cancer
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "This refers to tumours originating in the lung parenchyma or within the bronchi. Incidence is rising due to increase in smoking in both sexes, with nearly half of new cases diagnosed in the low income countries."
clinical_features[3]:
  - type: Local tumour effects
    features[6]: cough,breathlessness,haemoptysis,chest pain,weight loss,Horner syndrome
  - type: Distant metastasis
    features[3]: liver,bone,brain
  - type: Paraneoplastic syndrome
    features[5]: hypercalcemia,cushings's syndrome,hypoglycaemia,acromegaly,gynaecomastia
investigations[5]: Bronchoscopy plus biopsy,Mediastinoscopy,Thoracoscopy or video-assisted thoracoscopy,"Radiologic: chest radiograph, contrast-enhanced chest CT, PET-CT","Others: FBC, Electrolyte, Urea and Creatinine, LFT and Serum proteins"
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[0]:
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[0]:
prevention[3]: Avoidance of smoking including secondhand smoke,Reducing occupational exposure to lung carcinogens,Reduction of air pollution
other_investigations[4]: FBC,Electrolyte,Urea and Creatinine,LFT and Serum proteins
definitive_treatment[4]: "mainstay for stage I disease (wedge resection, segmentectomy, lobectomy, pneumonectomy, mediastinal node sampling)","Surgery + adjuvant chemotherapy: stages II and III disease","Palliative chemotherapy + radiotherapy: for stage IV disease","Targeted therapy: in selected cases (eg vascular endothelial growth factor inhibitor like bevacizumab)"
prognosis[0]: